Reason: every frame AM2R deactivates every solid in Samus's begin step and re-activates those near the view, and every
enemy's begin step calls instance_activate_region around itself; each call walks the room and recomputes the box of
every inactive instance, which has not changed (Collision_computeBBox was 2-5% of the CPU time in the profiled rooms,
Dolphin perf, plus its banker's roundings). An instance now remembers its last valid box together with every input the
computation reads: the resolved sprite index, the bits of x, y, both scales and the angle, that sprite's bbox mode,
margins, size and origin, and the collision compatibility mode. The box is reused only when all of them match, so it
is the box the computation would give; sprite_replace, a reused sprite slot or sprite_set_offset simply change the
key. Instances without a sprite are not remembered.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

